# ==============================================================================
# EVENTORA MONOREPO - VERCEL ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# ==============================================================================
# In Vercel Project Dashboard:
# Go to: Project Settings -> Environment Variables
# Add the following keys (select Production, Preview, Development):
#
# 1. MONGO_URI
#    Your MongoDB Atlas connection string:
#    mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/eventora?retryWrites=true&w=majority
#    *CRITICAL*: In MongoDB Atlas -> Network Access, whitelist 0.0.0.0/0 (Anywhere)
#
# 2. JWT_SECRET
#    A long random string, e.g.:
#    supersecretjwtkey_eventora_production_2026
#
# 3. EMAIL_USER (Optional - OTP prints to Vercel logs if not set)
#    your-email@gmail.com
#
# 4. EMAIL_PASS (Optional - 16-character Google App Password)
#    xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx
#
# 5. NODE_ENV
#    production
# ==============================================================================

MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/eventora?retryWrites=true&w=majority
JWT_SECRET=supersecretjwtkey_eventora_monorepo
EMAIL_USER=your_email@gmail.com
EMAIL_PASS=your_16_digit_app_password
NODE_ENV=development
